      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبْرَاجٌ</span></b>  A man <i>having that quality of the eye
which is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرَجٌ</span>: (M, TA:) fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرْجَآءُ</span>;
applied to a woman; (S) and also to an eye
(<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيْنٌ</span>) <i>having the quality termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرَجٌ</span>: (M, TA:)
pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُرْجٌ</span>. (Ham p. 560.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا أَبْرَجُ مِنْ هٰذَا</span> <i>This
is stronger than this.</i> (Har p. 286.)

